    {
      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "Using the distributive property, multiply each term in the first binomial by the second binomial.\n\nThus, ${(2x+3)(x+5) = 2x(x) + 2x(5) + 3(x) + 3(5)}$.\n\nNext, simply every term.\n\nSo, ${(2x+3)(x+5) = 2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15}$.\n\nAt this point, we need to factor the individual terms of the expression. To do that, write a product of the factors with the highest common monomial factor.\n\nThus, ${(2x+3)(x+5) = (2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15)} = (2x^2 + 13x + 15)}$.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is \\boxed{(2x^2 + 13x + 15)}.",
