    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Expansion can be done in any order.\n\nUsing the $(a+b)(c+d) = ac + ad + bc + bd$ or simply $(a+b)(c+d) = ac + ad + bc + bd$,\n\\begin{align*}\n&(2x+3)(x+5) \\\\\n&= 2x \\cdot x + 2x \\cdot 5 + 3 \\cdot x + 3 \\cdot 5 \\quad \\boxed{\\text{One could also use the $(a+b)(c+d) = ac + bd + ad + bc$ ordering}}\\\\\n&= 2x^2 + 10x + 3x + 15 \\qquad \\boxed{\\text{Simplifies}}\\\\\n&= 2x^2 + 13x + 15 \\qquad \\boxed{\\text{Final answer}}.\n\\end{align*}",
