    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve the given problem, we first need to expand the expression ${(2x+3)(x+5)}$. We can distribute each term in the first equation to each term in the second equation to get the product:\n\n(1) By commutative property, \"$+$\", and associativity property, we have:\n$$(2x+3)(x+5)=2x(x+5)+(3)(x+5).$$\n(2) Distribute $2x+a$ to the expression in $a$:\n$$(2x+a)(x+b)=(2x(x+b)+(x)(a))+{(a)(x+b)}$$\n(3) Simplify:\n$$(2x+a)(x+b)=2x(x+b)+(x+(a))+ab=2x^2+2x(x+b)+x+a+b.$$\nBy substituting the value of $x$ and $y$ from the question, we get the final answer: $\\boxed{13x+45}$.",
